
@startuml E3_API_02_MVC
title API 02: Wallet APIs (MVC view)

!theme plain
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 100
skinparam ranksep 90
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontSize 12

component "Core wallet API :5000\nGET /api/wallet/me\nGET /api/wallet/balance\nGET /api/wallet/transactions\nPOST /api/wallet/deposit\nPOST /api/wallet/withdraw\nGET /api/wallet/bank\nPOST /api/wallet/bank\nPOST /api/wallet/admin/adjust" as CoreApi <<REST API>>

component "Server_3 wallet proxy :4000\nGET /api/wallet/balance\nGET /api/wallet/transactions\nPOST /api/wallet/deposit\nPOST /api/wallet/withdraw\nGET /api/wallet/bank\nPOST /api/wallet/bank" as ProxyApi <<REST API>>

package "Server_3: request forwarding" {
  component "wallet.controller.js\nwithdrawalBank.controller.js" as ProxyCtrl <<Controller modules>>
  component "personA.gateway.js" as Gateway <<Gateway service>>
}

package "Core: authoritative wallet processing" {
  component "wallet.controller.js" as CoreCtrl <<Controller module>>
  component "wallet.service.js" as CoreService <<Service module>>
  component "ledger.service.js" as LedgerService <<Audit / ledger service>>
}

database "MySQL\nwallets, wallet_transactions,\nwithdrawal-bank records" as MySQL

package "Presentation (React)" {
  component "Wallet.jsx\nadmin/tabs/WalletOperations.jsx" as View <<View>>
  component "walletApi.js" as Adapter <<Frontend API module>>
}

View --> Adapter : invokes

Adapter --> CoreApi : GET balance / transactions\nPOST admin adjustment
Adapter --> ProxyApi : POST deposit / withdraw\nGET / POST bank details

ProxyApi --> ProxyCtrl : dispatch
ProxyCtrl --> Gateway : call
Gateway --> CoreApi : forwards 

CoreApi --> CoreCtrl : dispatch
CoreCtrl --> CoreService : validate and execute
CoreService --> MySQL :      reads/writes
CoreCtrl ..> LedgerService : best-effort ledger commit\nfor applicable mutations

note bottom of ProxyApi
  React uses Server_3 for bank details,
  deposits and withdrawals.
  Server_3 does not authoritatively
  settle these operations.
end note

note bottom of CoreApi
  React uses Core directly for wallet
  balance, transaction history,
  and admin adjustments.
  Core also exposes wallet routes
  used through the Server_3 proxy.
end note

@enduml
